<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yanam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yanam is a small town on the Godavari delta in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, enclosed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>. A French trading post from the 1720s, it remained part of French India until 1954, when it was transferred de facto to India, a transfer made legal in 1962. It is now a district of the Union Territory of Puducherry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yanam.jpg" alt="Yanam" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anand Deepak Racharla · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gowthami_river_Godavari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
